{"type":"standard","title":"Eric Sorensen (politician)","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Eric Sorensen (politician)</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q115182513","titles":{"canonical":"Eric_Sorensen_(politician)","normalized":"Eric Sorensen (politician)","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Eric Sorensen (politician)</span></span>"},"pageid":71179725,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Sorensen_House_Photo.jpg/330px-Sorensen_House_Photo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":411},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/34/Sorensen_House_Photo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2487,"height":3100},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1359547259","tid":"78584912-6905-11f1-a915-5bbb7784e9ee","timestamp":"2026-06-15T21:59:24Z","description":"American politician (born 1976)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eric_Sorensen_(politician)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eric_Sorensen_(politician)?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eric_Sorensen_(politician)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Eric_Sorensen_(politician)"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eric_Sorensen_(politician)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Eric_Sorensen_(politician)","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eric_Sorensen_(politician)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Eric_Sorensen_(politician)"}},"extract":"Eric Sorensen is an American politician and meteorologist serving as the U.S. representative for Illinois's 17th congressional district since 2023. His district covers a large swath of western and central Illinois, centered around Moline, Rock Island, and the Illinois side of the Quad Cities. It also includes parts of Peoria and Rockford. A member of the Democratic Party, Sorensen is the first openly gay member of Congress from Illinois.","extract_html":"<p><b>Eric Sorensen</b> is an American politician and meteorologist serving as the U.S. representative for Illinois's 17th congressional district since 2023. His district covers a large swath of western and central Illinois, centered around Moline, Rock Island, and the Illinois side of the Quad Cities. It also includes parts of Peoria and Rockford. A member of the Democratic Party, Sorensen is the first openly gay member of Congress from Illinois.</p>"}